Z||000000||reddog||11-08-2001||10:42 PM||||Does anyone know of a good site that can give me good instructions on replacing my stock injectors with the new tomco injectors that I got from the Fiero Store? Pics would be very helpful also!<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Picturenew_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||reddog||11-09-2001||12:33 AM||||anyone?<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Picturenew_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Neal||11-09-2001||12:58 AM||||It is EASY, pull off the upper plenum, vaccume lines, 2 bolts on the fuel rail and one on the cold start valve, 2 fuel lines.  The fuel rail can now be finessed/muscled out.  turn the clips on the fuel rail pull the injectors.  Assemble in the reverse order.||||reg||1
Z||000003||reddog||11-09-2001||01:35 AM||||Ok what about the cold start injector is it a seperate injector, a valve or what? I suspect it may be leaking. should it be replaced also or what. How do I check it, remove it all that stuff. I have found a switch but have not seen the actual valve for sale anywhere!<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Picturenew_sig.jpg">   <P>[This message has been edited by reddog (edited 11-09-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by reddog (edited 11-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||watts||11-09-2001||02:12 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by reddog:<BR><B>I have found a switch but have not seen the actual valve for sale anywhere!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That would probably be because you can't buy them (new) anymore.  Discontinued by GM a number of years ago.<BR><P>------------------<BR>87/88 V6 5spd Notchback Hybrid||||reg||1
Z||000005||Leadfoot||11-09-2001||10:55 AM||||Reddog I just did my 85 with tomco injectors and it is just like Neal said.  I did not change the colds start injector but I did replace the o-rings (P# 17111954). You can find the o-ring kit at carparts.com.  If you try the dealer you won't be able to get it.  However, the dealership still sells the cold start injector and tubing as does Napa.||||reg||1
